# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings on every platform, whatever core.autocrlf says
# (Git for Windows and the windows-latest runners default it to true). The conformance vectors, the
# fixture histories and the transparency vectors are compared byte for byte and hashed (MANIFEST.json),
# and a history or witness log with CRLF line endings is a different file (docs/PLATFORMS.md §5).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.tgz binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary

# A third-party license text kept exactly as its upstream ships it (CRLF).
brand/fonts/OFL-IBMPlex.txt -text
